(1155262, 143887, 28108, '<td valign="top">I know that might not have been the intention but she is giving the same stare/pose as the little girl on "Night of the Living Dead" movie poster. I like the back ground, maybe would have been a nice touch to clone out hole in the concrete on the upper right corner, I feel it''s distracting. The lightning is not bad exept for the shodowed eyes wich it give it a bit of grim look. I like a lot, I''m just not sure that was the intention looking at the shiny happy costume.</td>', 'I know that might not have been the intention but she is giving the same stare/pose as the little girl on "Night of the Living Dead" movie poster. I like the back ground, maybe would have been a nice touch to clone out hole in the concrete on the upper right corner, I feel it''s distracting. The lightning is not bad exept for the shodowed eyes wich it give it a bit of grim look. I like a lot, I''m just not sure that was the intention looking at the shiny happy costume.', '2005-02-07 15:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155266, 142707, 17103, '<td valign="top">I have to say that this photo is just awesome in my opinion.  The lighting is superb -- especially, as your title suggests, the light coming from within.  The composition and framing is simple and beautiful.  There''s just one little problem, and that is that I see no pink in the shot whatsoever!  It''s a gorgeous shade of peach, leaning heavily to the orange/red side, with some obvious golden yellow at the bottom of the bud, but no pink anywhere.  I checked this shot on two other monitors, by the way, because it would rate a 10 without question if I could see some pink in it, but no luck.  I''m still going to give it a 6 because it''s so good, and add it to my favorites, if that''s any consolation.</td>', 'I have to say that this photo is just awesome in my opinion.  The lighting is superb -- especially, as your title suggests, the light coming from within.  The composition and framing is simple and beautiful.  There''s just one little problem, and that is that I see no pink in the shot whatsoever!  It''s a gorgeous shade of peach, leaning heavily to the orange/red side, with some obvious golden yellow at the bottom of the bud, but no pink anywhere.  I checked this shot on two other monitors, by the way, because it would rate a 10 without question if I could see some pink in it, but no luck.  I''m still going to give it a 6 because it''s so good, and add it to my favorites, if that''s any consolation.', '2005-02-07 15:16:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155274, 143513, 17103, '<td valign="top">I do see some pink color in the center of the flower, but overall this shot doesn''t say "pink" to me as it''s overwhelmingly a bluish purple.  That said, I like the shot a lot.</td>', 'I do see some pink color in the center of the flower, but overall this shot doesn''t say "pink" to me as it''s overwhelmingly a bluish purple.  That said, I like the shot a lot.', '2005-02-07 15:18:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155278, 144050, 3697, '<td valign="top">I like your idea for the shot, and the focus is nice and clear. The only things I would change would be: zoom out a little bit, so that more of the golf tee can be seen and I would boost the contrast and saturation a wee bit. It''s still a good shot as is, and I hope my comment can be of some help :)</td>', 'I like your idea for the shot, and the focus is nice and clear. The only things I would change would be: zoom out a little bit, so that more of the golf tee can be seen and I would boost the contrast and saturation a wee bit. It''s still a good shot as is, and I hope my comment can be of some help :)', '2005-02-07 15:21:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155282, 143559, 17103, '<td valign="top">I really wish you hadn''t added the border.  The color of the buds clashes with it.  I''m not sure also if this would have worked a little better had there been more room on the top and bottom (not cropped so tightly vertically) or if the branch and buds had been angled a bit more.  Other than that, though, I like this shot a lot.</td>', 'I really wish you hadn''t added the border.  The color of the buds clashes with it.  I''m not sure also if this would have worked a little better had there been more room on the top and bottom (not cropped so tightly vertically) or if the branch and buds had been angled a bit more.  Other than that, though, I like this shot a lot.', '2005-02-07 15:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155285, 144334, 17103, '<td valign="top">While this shot is very pink, the color is actually a little too intense and is getting sort of blown out and causing a loss of detail.  I think this would have worked better had you decreased the saturation somewhat.</td>', 'While this shot is very pink, the color is actually a little too intense and is getting sort of blown out and causing a loss of detail.  I think this would have worked better had you decreased the saturation somewhat.', '2005-02-07 15:24:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155287, 143967, 2022, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition, nice colors, good lighting, one of my favorite pictures in this challenge, it should ribbon in my opinion. (10)</td>', 'Excellent composition, nice colors, good lighting, one of my favorite pictures in this challenge, it should ribbon in my opinion. (10)', '2005-02-07 15:25:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155289, 144468, 28108, '<td valign="top">This is very beautiful. I see a humanoid form in the drop. I wonder how many takes it would take me if I wanted to recreate it my-self. One of my top favorites in this beautiful challenge.</td>', 'This is very beautiful. I see a humanoid form in the drop. I wonder how many takes it would take me if I wanted to recreate it my-self. One of my top favorites in this beautiful challenge.', '2005-02-07 15:25:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155291, 144474, 17103, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot, but I have to say that in my opinion the dominant color is not pink but rather orange/red/peach.</td>', 'This is a great shot, but I have to say that in my opinion the dominant color is not pink but rather orange/red/peach.', '2005-02-07 15:26:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1155292, 144492, 15407, '<td valign="top">I like the shades of pink in this photo. It suggests to me that the nourshimernt from the flower is entering the Hummingbird. The dark background works very well and the lighting you created is particularly nice as it seems to originate within the sculpture, yet that could not be the case. Very well done, one of my favorites in this challenge,,,</td>', 'I like the shades of pink in this photo. It suggests to me that the nourshimernt from the flower is entering the Hummingbird. The dark background works very well and the lighting you created is particularly nice as it seems to originate within the sculpture, yet that could not be the case. Very well done, one of my favorites in this challenge,,,', '2005-02-07 15:26:17.000000', NULL, 1),
