(1182656, 144268, 7073, '<td valign="top">very dream like ... beautiful!</td>', 'very dream like ... beautiful!', '2005-02-19 18:35:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1183316, 143675, 10275, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the 12th finish Sally. It''s a very nice photo.</td>', 'Congrats on the 12th finish Sally. It''s a very nice photo.', '2005-02-20 02:01:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1183480, 144051, 33560, '<td valign="top">It''s an eye-catching shot.  I love the bright red bird and the dark background.  Who cares if the flamingo should be pink?  <br/> <br/>Is it possible that the edges were dodged to create that background?  And that the dodging went right to the edge of the feathers?  If not, what explains that glowing effect at most of the edges of the bird? In my eyes it takes a good point off the score of the shot.  <br/> <br/>Still, what you captured with the camera is super.</td>', 'It''s an eye-catching shot.  I love the bright red bird and the dark background.  Who cares if the flamingo should be pink?   Is it possible that the edges were dodged to create that background?  And that the dodging went right to the edge of the feathers?  If not, what explains that glowing effect at most of the edges of the bird? In my eyes it takes a good point off the score of the shot.   Still, what you captured with the camera is super.', '2005-02-20 09:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1183722, 144375, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>For the challenge I think this has been a little ''shoe-horned'' since the pink is forced, via editing, rather than present in the scene. That said, it''s a pleasant image and nicely balanced with the off-set composition. The key is good and it does have ''tissue box'' appeal.<br/> <br/>For me though, it does lack purpose and meaning - something that I like to find in a photo in order for me to hang it or return to it for repeat viewings.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', ':: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ For the challenge I think this has been a little ''shoe-horned'' since the pink is forced, via editing, rather than present in the scene. That said, it''s a pleasant image and nicely balanced with the off-set composition. The key is good and it does have ''tissue box'' appeal. For me though, it does lack purpose and meaning - something that I like to find in a photo in order for me to hang it or return to it for repeat viewings. CheersJon', '2005-02-20 12:49:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1183800, 144267, 15811, '<td valign="top">Thanks a lot sam.</td>', 'Thanks a lot sam.', '2005-02-20 13:49:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1183825, 144046, 31327, '<td valign="top">Dan<br/> <br/>I think this has a lot of obstacles. The eye is first drawn to the bright spot at the lower middle of the image, but there''s nothing to draw the eye away from it: the detailed are to the right lacks sufficient contrast or (focussed) detail to be of interest, and the line the cotton candy makes isn''t sharp enough to make the eye follow it.<br/> <br/>I think your shutter speeed was about a stop too slow to freeze the motion, which is why the image appears out of focus.<br/> <br/>I fear there''s nothing here to hold a viewer''s attention.</td>', 'Dan I think this has a lot of obstacles. The eye is first drawn to the bright spot at the lower middle of the image, but there''s nothing to draw the eye away from it: the detailed are to the right lacks sufficient contrast or (focussed) detail to be of interest, and the line the cotton candy makes isn''t sharp enough to make the eye follow it. I think your shutter speeed was about a stop too slow to freeze the motion, which is why the image appears out of focus. I fear there''s nothing here to hold a viewer''s attention.', '2005-02-20 14:13:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1184092, 141980, 31327, '<td valign="top">gina<br/> <br/>I have two criticisms of this image: the composition and the tocal range.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, the points of focus are the center of the roses; the lower right rose is well placed, but the left rose could be moved into the image more, to place it''s center in a more powerful position, and to eliminate that black space between the roses that prevents them from being one ''subject''. The frame could be opened to prevent the top of the frame from decapitating so much of the upper rose.<br/> <br/>Exposure-wise, this needs to be opened up a half stop or so. The colors suffer from desaturation, and the specular lights aren''t crisp enough. After lightening this image up, the details could be enhanced by tweaking the contrast.<br/> <br/>Just my thoughts.</td>', 'gina I have two criticisms of this image: the composition and the tocal range. Compositionally, the points of focus are the center of the roses; the lower right rose is well placed, but the left rose could be moved into the image more, to place it''s center in a more powerful position, and to eliminate that black space between the roses that prevents them from being one ''subject''. The frame could be opened to prevent the top of the frame from decapitating so much of the upper rose. Exposure-wise, this needs to be opened up a half stop or so. The colors suffer from desaturation, and the specular lights aren''t crisp enough. After lightening this image up, the details could be enhanced by tweaking the contrast. Just my thoughts.', '2005-02-20 16:56:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1184973, 143833, 34013, '<td valign="top">WOW. THIS IS BEAUTIFUL.  IM SPEECHLESS!</td>', 'WOW. THIS IS BEAUTIFUL.  IM SPEECHLESS!', '2005-02-20 23:34:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1185660, 144421, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>Well, this little fella isn''t going to win many beauty contests. Never mind. In his own way he is beautiful, just not typically so. He''s got cute eyes and an interesting nose, so we have something in common.<br/> <br/>As far as a critique goes, much has been already said below, but I classify this as a snapshot, so my critique as based around a shot that has no forward planning, set-up, pre-conceived ideas, etc.<br/> <br/>Good points:<br/>&gt; It''s well composed with the subject filling the frame<br/>&gt; Subject is unusual<br/>&gt; You''ve captured an elusive(?) creature<br/> <br/>Bad points:<br/>&gt; Flash has caused tonal imbalance<br/>&gt; Focus should be on eyes (stop down and you''d get more focal range, but low light would make this impractical with a moving subject)<br/>&gt; Colours are drab and uninteresting so it''s not appealing to most, apart from ''educational'' value<br/> <br/>Hope this helps<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', ':: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ Well, this little fella isn''t going to win many beauty contests. Never mind. In his own way he is beautiful, just not typically so. He''s got cute eyes and an interesting nose, so we have something in common. As far as a critique goes, much has been already said below, but I classify this as a snapshot, so my critique as based around a shot that has no forward planning, set-up, pre-conceived ideas, etc. Good points:> It''s well composed with the subject filling the frame> Subject is unusual> You''ve captured an elusive(?) creature Bad points:> Flash has caused tonal imbalance> Focus should be on eyes (stop down and you''d get more focal range, but low light would make this impractical with a moving subject)> Colours are drab and uninteresting so it''s not appealing to most, apart from ''educational'' value Hope this helps CheersJon', '2005-02-21 04:51:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1186282, 144009, 33736, '<td valign="top">Kylie,  <br/> <br/>I''d hitchhike to California if I thought you could make a picture of me look that good.  My chassis has changed designs many times over; pictorial history needs updating.<br/> <br/>There is a major difference between "Old" and "Classic" - you seem to have a talent for capturing the better of the two.  <br/> <br/>Kathy<br/> <br/>PS: There was no surprise in discovering that you receive one of the largest numbers of comments.  Terrific portfolio.</td>', 'Kylie,   I''d hitchhike to California if I thought you could make a picture of me look that good.  My chassis has changed designs many times over; pictorial history needs updating. There is a major difference between "Old" and "Classic" - you seem to have a talent for capturing the better of the two.   Kathy PS: There was no surprise in discovering that you receive one of the largest numbers of comments.  Terrific portfolio.', '2005-02-21 12:35:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1186794, 144521, 31637, '<td valign="top">This was just one of those photos I submitted purposely just to see how people react to it. It is an ugly photo, and the subject is not to appealing, and I know that. Brown Ribbon baby !! well deserved</td>', 'This was just one of those photos I submitted purposely just to see how people react to it. It is an ugly photo, and the subject is not to appealing, and I know that. Brown Ribbon baby !! well deserved', '2005-02-21 16:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
